{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788232992512215001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"balding-facial-huemul","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"81ae318912818b08df4ba5092aa21c07ebe251f6c0c971785e6dc36bd797f761","event_uuid":"2aa8ddc7-93fb-426e-9485-65a0ab7ccc50","position":{"commit_sha":"4a226c1051150fb413c51636e19e6e245916884d","position":"1788224470982895037-2aa8ddc7-93fb-426e-9485-65a0ab7ccc50"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788224470982895037,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Problem\n\nEvery COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar is emitted with `material=None` — `completion_sidecar.emit(result, material=None, repo_root=repo_root)` at `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:405`, with the comment at `:754` noting no fingerprint is computed on this path. Measured on the live store: 0 of the most recent 300 COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (216 PASS / 59 FAIL / 23 no-verdict / 2 ERROR) carry any material/material_fingerprint field.\n\n## Consequence (why this is worth fixing)\n\nA FAIL followed by a PASS on the same `verified_at_sha` cannot be attributed: verifier inputs include ticket comments and prefetched evidence, which change without a code commit, so \"no commit in between\" does not mean \"same inputs.\" This makes the completion gate's precision unmeasurable from its own records (an analysis this week mis-derived an \"80–84% FP\" figure from exactly this gap), and it means completion attestations cannot support the stale-material currency discipline that plan-review attestations already have.\n\nNote: the `material=None` is deliberate per the code's own comment — this ticket treats the capability gap as the defect (operator-directed filing, 2026-08-31). Formula/prompt version stamping in the same record would make longitudinal gate analysis version-aware (pass-3 blocking formulas have changed over time, so unversioned sidecars conflate formula eras).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecars (PASS, FAIL, ERROR alike) record a material fingerprint over the verifier's actual inputs (ticket material as pinned for the run: description/ACs/comments snapshot + evidence set identifiers), reusing the existing plan-review fingerprint machinery where applicable rather than inventing a new scheme.\n- [ ] Sidecars record the verifier formula/prompt version identifier alongside the fingerprint.\n- [ ] Existing sidecars are untouched (no backfill); consumers treat absent material as \"unknown era\".\n- [ ] A regression test asserts a FAIL sidecar carries a non-null fingerprint and version.\n\n## File impact\n\nTo be confirmed at investigation (bugs do not pre-declare impact): expected `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`, `src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py` (or equivalent emitter), one test module.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e4a5-1e8e-e441-43a3","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion-verifier sidecars carry no material fingerprint, so FAIL->PASS transitions cannot be attributed","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2aa8ddc7-93fb-426e-9485-65a0ab7ccc50"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788232992512215001,"uuid":"e1ca8d7f-e665-4d1f-b7c6-2c770972329a"}